OL,3,GNEWSAMove to fine excess or damaging
OL,4,Abranchages
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople cutting hedges and banks
OL,7,F"excessively" or causing "lasting
OL,8,Fdamage" during Jersey's branchage could
OL,9,Fbe fined in the future.
OL,11,FThe branchage has been in place since
OL,12,F1914 to try to ensure public roads are
OL,13,Fnot obstructed by overgrowth, with a
OL,14,Frule ensuring a 12ft (3.6m) clearance
OL,15,Fover main roads and by-roads and an 8ft
OL,16,F(2.4m) clearance over footpaths.
OL,18,FIn September, the chair of the
OL,19,Fconstables committee Constable Andy
OL,20,FJehan said the 111-year-old law was
OL,21,Fbeing reviewed.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
